<title>USA: U.S. and Australia agree on antitrust pact.</title>
<headline>U.S. and Australia agree on antitrust pact.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States and Australia have reached agreement to exchange evidence on antitrust investigations, American officials announced Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The proposed agreement between the U.S. and Australia, which we hope will be the first of many with other countries, will help us to protect consumers and the business community,&quot; said Federal Trade Commission Chairman Robert Pitofsky said.</p>
<p>Joel Klein, acting assistant attorney general in charge of the antitrust division of the Justice Department, said the agreement would make it easier for him to go after international cartels.</p>
</text>
